TI  - Plasmodium falciparum drug resistance in Angola.
PG  - 74
LID - 10.1186/s12936-016-1122-z [doi]
LID - 74
AB  - Facing chloroquine drug resistance, Angola promptly adopted artemisinin-based 
      combination therapy as the first-line to treat malaria. Currently, the country 
      aims to consolidate malaria control, while preparing for the elimination of the 
      disease, along with others African countries in the region. However, the 
      remarkable capacity of Plasmodium to develop drug resistance represents an 
      alarming threat for those achievements. Herein, the available, but relatively 
      scarce and dispersed, information on malaria drug resistance in Angola, is 
      reviewed and discussed. The review aims to inform but also to encourage future 
      research studies that monitor and update the information on anti-malarial drug 
      efficacy and prevalence of molecular markers of drug resistance, key fields in 
      the context and objectives of elimination.
