TI  - [Artemisinin resistance in Plasmodium falciparum: global status and basic 
      research].
PG  - 380-4
AB  - Artemisinin-resistant Plasmodium falciparum has been identified by WHO in the 
      Greater Mekong subregion. While there is no report on artemisinin resistance in 
      Africa and South America by now, related surveillance measures have been taken 
      place. The genes related artemisinin-resistance has been identified and the 
      molecular markers will be used for large-scale surveillance efforts to contain 
      artemisinin resistance. The emergence and spread of artemisinin resistance 
      worldwide is a present danger and needs more attention. This article reviews the 
      progress of artemisininresistance malaria parasites and artemisinin-based 
      combination therapies.
